257
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:33,290
It's scary.

258
00:13:33,373 --> 00:13:35,777
Whatever you do, don't
be afraid, okay, guys?

259
00:13:35,860 --> 00:13:38,657
I've realized that it's your
fear that feeds the darkness.

260
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:40,328
That's easy for you to say.

261
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:47,000
Are you all right, Joe?

262
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:51,697
Yeah, fortunately I landed on the one part
of my body that has a built-in airbag.

263
00:13:51,780 --> 00:13:52,610
Very funny.

264
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:53,970
Where's Sora?

265
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:55,060
We need a clue.

266
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:58,877
Listen, I think I hear something
coming from over there.

267
00:13:58,960 --> 00:13:59,790
Huh?

268
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:02,195
I'd call that a clue.

269
00:14:07,820 --> 00:14:09,400
Sora, talk to me.

270
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,097
Please tell me what's wrong.

271
00:14:11,180 --> 00:14:12,474
That's Violon's voice.

272
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,736
Which means Sora can't be far behind.

273
00:14:15,940 --> 00:14:17,240
Sora, Sora.

274
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:21,060
Hang on, Violon. We're coming. Over here.

275
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:27,860
Sora, what's the matter with you? Get up.

276
00:14:29,980 --> 00:14:32,360
She's stuck. Let me help. On three.

277
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:34,100
One, two, three.

278
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:40,917
Once, it took four of us to get my
grandmother off the toilet like that.

279
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:41,830
Hey, listen.

280
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:43,760
Sora's saying something. Huh?

281
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:46,700
I have to find Mimi and Joe and Matt.

282
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:50,000
I have to help Tai or the
world will be destroyed.

283
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:52,660
There's no place like home.

284
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:54,640
There's no place like home.

285
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:56,697
She won't talk to me anymore.

286
00:14:56,780 --> 00:14:59,877
All she does is keep mumbling the
same thing over and over again.

287
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:03,300
Sora, Matt and I are right
here. Look at me. Focus.

288
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:05,512
Joe, you're really here.

289
00:15:05,660 --> 00:15:06,920
I can't believe it.

290
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:09,211
And Matt's with you, too.

291
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:10,630
Just relax.

292
00:15:10,713 --> 00:15:12,117
Everything's going to be okay now.

293
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,237
I'm afraid not.

294
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:15,237
I haven't been trying hard enough.

295
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:17,897
I have to get to Tai right
away and help him fight.

296
00:15:17,980 --> 00:15:21,437
Because if I don't, the world
will be completely destroyed.

297
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:22,350
Sora, come on.

298
00:15:22,433 --> 00:15:24,397
You can't be responsible
for saving the world.

299
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:26,997
You have to realize how strong
your negative feelings are.

300
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,737
They produce a powerful,
destructive energy.

301
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:32,677
Sora, it's the darkness in your heart that
has created the cave in the first place.

302
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:33,590
Don't you get it?

303
00:15:33,673 --> 00:15:34,503
Really, Matt?

304
00:15:34,586 --> 00:15:35,416
Is that true?

305
00:15:35,499 --> 00:15:37,377
Is that why you told TK not to be scared?

306
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:38,497
Sora, listen to me.

307
00:15:38,580 --> 00:15:41,357
There's only one way to
make this cave disappear.

308
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:46,120
You've got to reach deep into your heart
and erase all the negative feelings.

309
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:49,360
I don't know if I can.

310
00:15:51,720 --> 00:15:52,840
What should I do?

311
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:56,749
You'll have to find the answer
to that question on your own.

312
00:15:57,160 --> 00:16:00,397
Sora, this isn't the kind of thing
you do just because you have to.

313
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:04,177
If you're going to do it, then
it has to be because you want to.

314
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:07,457
You mean that I don't have
to do it if I don't want to?

315
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:08,370
Right.

316
00:16:08,453 --> 00:16:10,157
It'll only work if you want to do it.

317
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:11,120
I'm confused.

318
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:15,146
How will I know what the
right thing to do is?

319
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:16,717
When this whole thing started,

320
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:19,337
do you think we had any idea
what the right thing to do was?

321
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:20,250
Of course not.

322
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:21,937
But that didn't stop us, did it?

323
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:23,557
Maybe we're here for a reason.

324
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:25,993
Maybe we're the only ones who can do it.

325
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:33,197
We're the only ones who
can make a difference.

326
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:34,297
It's working, Matt.

327
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:36,277
I think we're finally
getting through to her.

328
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,800
We're the only ones.

329
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:39,954
That's why we're here.

330
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:46,610
Huh?

331
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,060
I get it now.

332
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:50,437
You were right, Matt.

333
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:51,520
How did you know?

334
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:54,157
I kind of went through
the same thing myself.

335
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:55,100
Welcome back.

336
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:02,814
I'm so happy that you're the
old Sora, not the new Sora.

337
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:05,700
The cave's gone.

338
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:09,764
When the darkness from Sora's
heart disappeared, so did the cave.

339
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:11,880
I feel so relieved.

340
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,859
Boy, wait till Tai hears about this.

341
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:16,382
Let's find him.

342
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:18,245
Ty's waiting for us right now.

343
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:19,330
Let's go.

344
00:17:20,220 --> 00:17:21,050
Right.

345
00:17:21,600 --> 00:17:22,430
Trump's all.

346
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:29,960
Get up, Tai! Hey, Tai!

347
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:31,340
Izzy, stop!

348
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:34,940
You stay there! Protect Kari!

349
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:41,730
Tai, look.

350
00:17:41,813 --> 00:17:44,117
I know it's important for me
to stay here and protect Kari,

351
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,997
but in the meantime, who's
going to protect you?

352
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:47,937
He tends to be a bit stubborn, doesn't he?

353
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:50,120
Don't worry about me. I'm fine.

354
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:52,277
I've got him right where I want him.

355
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,280
He's exhausted.

356
00:17:53,660 --> 00:17:54,900
But I can help you.

357
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:59,200
I'm fine. That's funny.

358
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:02,177
General Custer said the exact
same thing at Little Bighorn.

359
00:18:02,260 --> 00:18:04,025
Thanks for the history lesson.

360
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:05,261
All right, then.

361
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:06,242
Just one thing.

362
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:10,007
